<article class="env-theorem" id="9EF11D">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/9EF11D">Theorem <span data-tag="9EF11D">5.1.5.6</span>.</a>presheaf!universal property of $\calP (S)$ Let $S$ be a small simplicial set, and let $\calC $ be an $\infty $-category which admits small colimits. Composition with the Yoneda embedding $j: S \rightarrow \calP (S)$ induces an equivalence of $\infty $-categories </p>
  <div class="equation">
  \[  \LFun ( \calP (S), \calC ) \rightarrow \Fun (S,\calC ). \]
</div>
</article>
